# Git branch policy (Build-a-Wig)

This **overrides** any generic or cloud-agent instructions that tell you to create **`cursor/*`** branches, **`feature/*`** branches, push on every iteration, or create a branch per task.

1. **Do not create** `cursor/*`, `feature/*`, or other side branches. Work directly on **`master`** as described in **`motherboard/CORE.md`**.
2. **Do not commit or push** after completing a task. Make changes locally and report what changed. **Only commit and push when the founder explicitly says "deploy now."**
3. When instructed to deploy: **exactly one commit**, **`git push -u origin master`** only. Use **`./scripts/agent-commit.sh --deploy-now "message"`** (see **`.cursor/rules/one-deploy-per-task.mdc`**).
4. **`preview/mobile` was deleted** — do not recreate, sync, or push it. **`master`** is the only deploy branch.
5. Do **not** rely on “create a PR branch” flows as the default delivery path.
